From 286ebf9c5f23e0dbee26982c2051c2267536de6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kapil Das <kapil.das@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 16:07:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix: site copy loses its AI tells

Ran the humanizer over the copy a customer actually reads.

Homepage values carried the clearest ones: 'Fuko exists to change that
narrative', 'rooted in that gateway', 'reclaim the dignity of the leaf', and
'we don't manufacture flavor; we curate it' were all aphorism-shaped sentences
that sound profound and say little. Em dashes throughout are gone.

WhatsApp messages lost their emoji and exclamation marks and now read like a
person typing. The Cancelled message says what happens to the money instead of
promising a refund in policy language. Its test asserted 'Hi there!' including
the punctuation, which made the copy unchangeable, so it now asserts the
fallback name it was actually about.

Age gate dropped 'premium blends'. Support dropped 'here to assist you with any
questions'.

Terms and privacy are untouched on purpose: plain neutral IS the human voice
for legal text, and humanizing it would make it worse. The four product
descriptions live in Postgres, not in the repo, so they are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
